From: Lecithin <noreply@lophinelabs.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:40:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] load every fork's lang namespace, not just this one

The loader hard-coded /assets/lophine/lang/<lang>.json, so a downstream fork
shipping its own lang files - under the namespace its own contributing guide
tells contributors to use, and the namespace ConfigsInstance already assumes
when it builds a comment key as "<config instance name>.<key path>.comment" -
had them silently never loaded. Measured: lecithin_global_config.toml is
generated with no comments at all while lophine_global_config.toml has them.

The namespaces are now discovered from the class path: every assets/<ns>/lang
directory that is not a vanilla one. That is order-independent, which matters
because Language.DEFAULT_INSTANCE is built in a static initialiser that can run
before the config system exists, so a registry populated at startup would be
empty exactly when it is first read. It is also generic in the way a registry
would not be: no fork name, plugin name or resource path appears in this class.

minecraft and realms are excluded deliberately. createLangInstance loads the
downloaded vanilla file for the requested language first, so re-reading the
English assets/minecraft/lang/en_us.json that ships in the jar would overwrite
every translated vanilla string with English again.

If enumeration fails entirely - a class path this code cannot walk - it falls
back to the single namespace it used before, so the worst case is today's
behaviour rather than no localized comments at all.

loadLophineI18nDefault is kept as a deprecated delegate because
net.minecraft.locale.Language calls it by that name; renaming it would add a
minecraft patch for one line.

